  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Write down the coordinates of the vertex and state the concavity for each parabola. Hence determine the number of $x$-intercepts.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=2(x-3)^2-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertex $(3,-5)$; concave up; two $x$-intercepts.",
          "worked": "In $y=a(x-h)^2+k$, the vertex is $(h,k)$. Here the vertex is $(3,-5)$ and $a=2>0$, so the parabola is concave up. Its vertex lies below the $x$-axis, so there are two $x$-intercepts.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-3(x+2)^2-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertex $(-2,-1)$; concave down; no $x$-intercepts.",
          "worked": "Since $x+2=x-(-2)$, the vertex is $(-2,-1)$. Here $a=-3<0$, so the parabola is concave down. Its maximum value is $-1$, below the $x$-axis, so there are no $x$-intercepts.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$y=4(x+1)^2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Vertex $(-1,0)$; concave up; one $x$-intercept.",
          "worked": "Since $x+1=x-(-1)$, the vertex is $(-1,0)$. Here $a=4>0$, so the parabola is concave up. Its vertex lies on the $x$-axis, so it touches the axis once, at $(-1,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
